---
title: Tactile display — how a chart becomes pins
---
%% Verified against the tree on 2026-08-28.
%% The native layer is behind IDotPadNative, so the driver and its paging logic are
%% testable off-Windows against NullDotPadNative; only WindowsDotPadNative P/Invokes.
graph TD
    subgraph CORE["AccessibleTrader.Core"]
        HB["History buffer — the full Ohlcv series"]
        TCC["TactileCanvasCoordinator<br/>decides WHAT gets a pane"]
        VC["Virtual canvas — the whole chart at pin resolution"]
        VP["ViewportManager<br/>slices the device-sized window"]
        GTR["GraphicTextRenderer<br/>value strip + X-value strip"]
    end

    subgraph DRIVER["Driver — ITactileDriver"]
        DTD["DotpadTactileDriver<br/>two-pane 50/50: top series + focused series,<br/>1-pin candles, dynamic gap by bar density"]
        IFACE["IDotPadNative"]
        WIN["WindowsDotPadNative<br/>P/Invoke to DotPadSDK-3.0.0.dll"]
        NULL["NullDotPadNative<br/>everywhere else — driver logic stays testable"]
    end

    subgraph HW["Hardware"]
        PD["Dot Pad — 300 graphic cells + 20 braille cells<br/>2nd generation (tested on device) and Dot Pad X<br/>same SDK, no code change"]
    end

    HB --> TCC --> VC
    VC -->|paging| VP
    VP -->|device-sized window| DTD
    GTR --> DTD
    DTD --> IFACE
    IFACE --> WIN --> PD
    IFACE -.-> NULL

    PD -->|pan and function keys| WIN
    WIN -->|key callback| DTD
    DTD -->|F1-F4 device-side speech queries| GTR
    DTD -->|navigate| VP
    VP -->|new window offset| VC

    NOTE["F4 toggles the display, Shift+F4 opens its settings.<br/>Driver is Windows-only today; the SDK is not committed to the repo.<br/>Other tactile devices (APH Monarch and the rest) are not supported yet."]
